{
  "kind": "Dashboard",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "thalamus_usage",
    "project": "workload-management"
  },
  "spec": {
    "display": {
      "name": "Thalamus Usage"
    },
    "variables": [
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Rate Interval",
            "hidden": false
          },
          "value": "15m",
          "name": "rate_interval"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Quantile",
            "hidden": false
          },
          "value": "0.99",
          "name": "quantile"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Rate Multiplier (per-second → per-hour = 3600)",
            "hidden": false
          },
          "value": "1",
          "name": "rate_multiplier"
        }
      }
    ],
    "panels": {
      "readme": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "README"
          },
          "plugin": {
            "kind": "Markdown",
            "spec": {
              "text": "# Thalamus Usage\n\n## Description\n\nHow users interact with the vLLM deployments in `thalamus`: how many requests, how many tokens in and out, what parameters clients send. This is load and shape — not performance. For latency/SLO signals see the SLO dashboard; for internal debugging see Debug/vLLM.\n\nAll rate/throughput panels have a **total** series first, then per-`model_name` series. All histograms are **rounded** (`round(histogram_quantile(...))`) because token counts and `n`/`max_tokens` are inherently integer.\n\n## Variables\n\n- `$rate_interval` (default `15m`) — smoothing window for `rate()` on counters. Wider = smoother, hides bursts.\n- `$quantile` (default `0.99`) — which percentile the histogram panels display. Change to `0.5` to see the median.\n- `$rate_multiplier` (default `1`) — `rate()` always outputs per-second; set to `3600` for per-hour, `60` for per-minute. Change the y-axis label to match if you flip this.\n\n## Panels\n\n### Tokens section\n\n#### Prompt Tokens/sec\nInput tokens the model is processing, per second.\n\nQuery: `sum(rate(vllm:prompt_tokens_total[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier` (+ per-model).\n\n`rate()` on a counter (monotonically increasing number) returns per-second increase averaged over the window.\n\n**Debug scenario:** Prompt tokens/sec drops to zero. Either no traffic is arriving (check `Success Rate` — also flat?) or the scrape is broken (check the Prometheus target). Rising suddenly with `Success Rate` flat → clients are sending bigger prompts, not more requests; correlate with `Input Tokens` p99 and Debug/vLLM `Prefill Time`.\n\n#### Prompt Tokens by Source\nSplit by `source` label: `computed` (had to be processed) vs `cache_hit` (served from KV cache — no compute cost).\n\nQuery: `sum by (source) (rate(vllm:prompt_tokens_by_source_total[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier`\n\n**Debug scenario:** All traffic shows `source=computed` even though clients reuse the same system prompt on every request. Prefix cache is not working — likely block-size mismatch or the shared prefix is shorter than one KV block. Confirm with Debug/vLLM `Prefix Cache Hit Ratio`; when fixed, `cache_hit` share here should climb.\n\n#### Generation Tokens/sec\nOutput tokens the model is generating.\n\nQuery: `sum(rate(vllm:generation_tokens_total[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier` (+ per-model).\n\n**Debug scenario:** Prompt tokens/sec at 10k, generation at 200. Most requests either return short answers or die before generating. Open `Request Outcomes`: if `error` or `abort` is elevated, model or clients are failing early; if `stop` dominates, users are asking questions with short answers — not a bug.\n\n#### Input Tokens (p99 by default)\nDistribution of **prompt size per request**. Uses `llm_d_epp_request_input_tokens` (endpoint picker view), which has finer high-end bucket resolution than vLLM's histogram — so long prompts show accurate values rather than clamping at vLLM's top bucket.\n\nQuery: `round(histogram_quantile($quantile, sum by (target_model_name, le) (rate(llm_d_epp_request_input_tokens_bucket[$rate_interval]))))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** p99 jumps from 800 to 3200. Someone shipped a new client that stuffs a huge context in every request. This will show up in Debug/vLLM `Prefill Time` p99 climbing and SLO `TTFT` p99 breaching within minutes. Cross-check with Debug/vLLM `Prompt Token Distribution` — if that panel is stuck at its top bucket while this one shows the real value, you're seeing vLLM histogram clamping in action.\n\n#### Output Tokens (p99 by default)\nDistribution of **generation size per request**.\n\nQuery: `round(histogram_quantile($quantile, sum by (target_model_name, le) (rate(llm_d_epp_request_output_tokens_bucket[$rate_interval]))))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** p99 sits exactly at the client's `max_tokens`. Requests are being cut off mid-answer. Either raise `max_tokens` (check `Requested max_tokens`) or accept the truncation. Confirm by looking at `Request Outcomes` for a spike in `finished_reason=length`.\n\n#### Total Tokens Generated (table)\nAbsolute count of generation tokens over the dashboard's selected time range, per model plus a `Total` row.\n\nQuery: `round(sum by (model_name) (increase(vllm:generation_tokens_total[$__range]))) or label_replace(round(sum(increase(...))), \"model_name\", \"Total\", \"\", \"\")`\n\n`increase()` = the counter's total delta over `$__range` (the visible time window). Useful for capacity accounting and cost reporting.\n\n**Debug scenario:** Reporting for a monthly review — set the dashboard time range to the month, read the `Total` row. Or: one model shows zero over the last hour while others are active → that model has no traffic (paused deployment, misrouted clients, or wrong model name in requests).\n\n### Requests section\n\n#### Success Rate\nCompleted requests per second. Filtered to `finished_reason=~\"stop|length\"` to exclude errors/aborts.\n\nQuery: `sum(rate(vllm:request_success_total{finished_reason=~\"stop|length\"}[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier` (+ per-model).\n\n`finished_reason=stop` = model produced a natural stop token. `length` = hit `max_tokens`.\n\n**Debug scenario:** Success rate on model A drops to zero while model B stays flat. Open `Running Requests` — if A has zero there too, no traffic is reaching it (routing issue, deployment scaled to 0, model name mismatch). If `Running Requests` is non-zero but success is zero, requests are entering but erroring out — check `Error Rate` and `Request Outcomes`.\n\n#### Error Rate\nFailed requests per second: `finished_reason=~\"abort|error\"`.\n\nQuery: same shape as `Success Rate` with the abort/error filter.\n\nThe metric name is `request_success_total` — misleading, but that's where errors are counted on this vLLM version (there is no `request_failure_total`).\n\n**Debug scenario:** Error rate spikes right after a rollout. Check pod logs and `Request Outcomes` split — `error` = model server fault (bad config, OOM, crash-looping), `abort` = clients disconnecting (timeouts on their side, cancellations). If it's `abort`, latency is likely also up in the SLO dashboard.\n\n#### Running Requests\nHow many requests are currently in prefill or decode across all pods.\n\nQuery: `sum(vllm:num_requests_running)` (+ per-model). Gauge — no `rate()`.\n\n**Debug scenario:** Value pegged at a constant (say 128) for hours while `Queue Depth` (SLO) climbs. vLLM has hit its `max_num_seqs` limit — every new request queues. Either raise `max_num_seqs`, scale replicas, or accept the queueing.\n\n#### Requested n\nDistribution of the `n` request parameter (completions per request). p99 by default.\n\nQuery: `round(histogram_quantile($quantile, sum by (model_name, le) (rate(vllm:request_params_n_bucket[$rate_interval]))))`\n\n**Debug scenario:** GPU dashboard shows saturation but Usage `Prompt Tokens/sec` is flat — where is the load coming from? Check here: p99 jumping from 1 to 4 means each request now does 4× the GPU work. One client changed their SDK defaults.\n\n#### Requested max_tokens\nDistribution of client-requested `max_tokens`. p99 by default.\n\nQuery: `round(histogram_quantile($quantile, sum by (model_name, le) (rate(vllm:request_params_max_tokens_bucket[$rate_interval]))))`\n\nThis is what clients **ask for**. What vLLM actually caps at is in Debug/vLLM `Max Generation Tokens` — compare them.\n\n**Debug scenario:** p99 jumps to 32768. One client is asking for 32k tokens on every call, even for short questions. `Generation Tokens/sec` will spike, GPU decode time will climb. Talk to that client's owner.\n\n#### Request Outcomes\nRequests per second broken down by `finished_reason` label (`stop`, `length`, `abort`, `error`).\n\nQuery: `sum by (finished_reason) (rate(vllm:request_success_total[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier`\n\n**Debug scenario:** `length` share rises sharply. Users are hitting `max_tokens` more often — either their prompts are eliciting longer answers, or their `max_tokens` setting was lowered. Cross-check `Output Tokens` p99 (should sit at the cap). Fix: raise `max_tokens` or warn users.\n"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "success_rate": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Success Rate"
          },
          "plugin": {
            "kind": "TimeSeriesChart",
            "spec": {
              "legend": {
                "mode": "table",
                "position": "right",
                "size": "small",
                "values": ["last"]
              },
              "visual": {
                "areaOpacity": 0.2,
                "connectNulls": false,
                "display": "line",
                "lineStyle": "solid",
                "lineWidth": 1.5,
                "pointRadius": 2
              },
              "yAxis": {
                "format": { "unit": "decimal" },
                "label": "req/s",
                "min": 0,
                "show": true
              }
            }
          },
          "queries": [
            {
              "kind": "TimeSeriesQuery",
              "spec": {
                "plugin": {
                  "kind": "PrometheusTimeSeriesQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "datasource": { "kind": "PrometheusDatasource", "name": "kube-monitoring-prometheus" },
                    "query": "sum(rate(vllm:request_success_total{finished_reason=~\"stop|length\"}[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier",
                    "seriesNameFormat": "total"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "TimeSeriesQuery",
              "spec": {
                "plugin": {
                  "kind": "PrometheusTimeSeriesQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "datasource": { "kind": "PrometheusDatasource", "name": "kube-monitoring-prometheus" },
                    "query": "sum by (model_name) (rate(vllm:request_success_total{finished_reason=~\"stop|length\"}[$rate_interval])) * $rate_multiplier",
                    "seriesNameFormat": "{{model_name}}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "error_rate": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "display": {
            "name": "Error Rate"
          },
          "plugin": {
            "kind": "TimeSeriesChart",
